## No context-size gate for router downgrades

All cheap-class subagent/router downgrades target the real `deepseek-v4-flash` (via `defaultFlashModel`, OpenRouter equivalent only during peak) which has 1M context and fast cached prefill; there is no performance-based reason to skip downgrades based on context size, unlike the old glm-4.7 lane model.

